00:01:23.065 --> 00:01:26.898
- Tomorrow, some day,
next week, I'm about to.

00:01:28.952 --> 00:01:33.224
This is the language that I
hear a lot in network marketing.

00:01:33.224 --> 00:01:34.992
Tomorrow I'm going to get started.

00:01:34.992 --> 00:01:37.720
Tomorrow I'm going to
schedule some appointments.

00:01:37.720 --> 00:01:40.457
After the weekend I'm
really going to kick it.

00:01:40.457 --> 00:01:44.551
When the new month starts,
I'm going to make it happen.

00:01:44.551 --> 00:01:46.688
Once I get past this birthday,

00:01:46.688 --> 00:01:48.949
then I'm really going to take off.

00:01:48.949 --> 00:01:51.218
Once the kids get out of school,

00:01:51.218 --> 00:01:52.732
then I'm going to focus on this.

00:01:52.732 --> 00:01:56.659
Once the kids get back into
school, after the summer break,

00:01:56.659 --> 00:01:57.492
then I'm going to do it.

00:01:57.492 --> 00:02:02.156
After the holidays, then
I'm going to make it happen.

00:02:02.156 --> 00:02:03.851
Now here's the thing.

00:02:03.851 --> 00:02:07.482
People do a lot of talking,
and one side of proclaiming

00:02:07.482 --> 00:02:09.039
what you're going to do is very good,

00:02:09.039 --> 00:02:11.761
telling the world what you're about to do.

00:02:11.761 --> 00:02:14.152
Telling them something
that you haven't done yet,

00:02:14.152 --> 00:02:16.654
that's a very healthy
thing 'cause it'll hold you

00:02:16.654 --> 00:02:20.821
accountable to those statements,
but don't get stuck there.

00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:23.758
Don't stay in tomorrow,

00:02:24.918 --> 00:02:29.085
you've got to at some point
move from tomorrow to right now.

00:02:32.472 --> 00:02:35.088
Move from the action that
you're going to do on Monday,

00:02:35.088 --> 00:02:36.106
to right now.

00:02:36.106 --> 00:02:39.381
Not even today, because
that gives you all the time

00:02:39.381 --> 00:02:41.054
until the end of the day.

00:02:41.054 --> 00:02:43.471
You've got to move your clock,

00:02:44.783 --> 00:02:47.204
when you think about here's
one thing I need to do,

00:02:47.204 --> 00:02:48.858
I need to schedule more appointments,

00:02:48.858 --> 00:02:51.467
I'm going to do that right now.

00:02:51.467 --> 00:02:54.375
Right now, the first available
moment I have to do it,

00:02:54.375 --> 00:02:55.350
I'm going to do it right now.

00:02:55.350 --> 00:02:58.596
I'm going to start right now, I'm
going to get moving right now.

00:02:58.596 --> 00:03:00.203
Because a lot of you are
listening to this stuff,

00:03:00.203 --> 00:03:02.364
and that's great, listening is great.

00:03:02.364 --> 00:03:04.624
Understanding is even better,

00:03:04.624 --> 00:03:08.041
action is even better than understanding.

00:03:09.498 --> 00:03:11.632
You can have the most
knowledgeable person in the world,

00:03:11.632 --> 00:03:15.723
but if they keep saying tomorrow
tomorrow tomorrow tomorrow,

00:03:15.723 --> 00:03:17.590
they're never going to get the results

00:03:17.590 --> 00:03:18.464
that they're looking for,

00:03:18.464 --> 00:03:20.393
so guess where most of the learning

00:03:20.393 --> 00:03:23.509
and most of the real
understanding comes from.

00:03:23.509 --> 00:03:24.994
In the doing.

00:03:24.994 --> 00:03:26.924
A lot of people think that
they understand network

00:03:26.924 --> 00:03:31.068
marketing, and they can
never understand what it is

00:03:31.068 --> 00:03:35.404
that you do every day because
they've never done it.

00:03:35.404 --> 00:03:39.571
You understand, really, on a
cellular level, when you do it.

00:03:41.221 --> 00:03:44.778
And if you continue with
action, you'll start

00:03:44.778 --> 00:03:48.417
to get results from those actions.

00:03:48.417 --> 00:03:50.198
'Cause it's not just in the doing once,

00:03:50.198 --> 00:03:51.615
it's the doing and then refining,

00:03:51.615 --> 00:03:53.660
and doing again and then refining.

00:03:53.660 --> 00:03:56.399
Work getting better every single day.

00:03:56.399 --> 00:03:58.140
Understanding that you can't look good

00:03:58.140 --> 00:03:59.515
and get better at the same time.

00:03:59.515 --> 00:04:01.532
Being willing to be uncomfortable,

00:04:01.532 --> 00:04:03.806
being willing to get outside
of your comfort zone.

00:04:03.806 --> 00:04:07.674
Being willing to go from a tomorrow person

00:04:07.674 --> 00:04:09.507
to a right now person.

00:04:10.498 --> 00:04:14.831
My future plan is about this thick, typed.

00:04:14.831 --> 00:04:18.383
It's usually about 40 page or so,

00:04:18.383 --> 00:04:20.694
and it includes everything.

00:04:20.694 --> 00:04:24.230
And today more than ever, what
you'll find with top leaders,

00:04:24.230 --> 00:04:26.954
what you'll find with successful people,

00:04:26.954 --> 00:04:30.948
is they're forward thinking,
they're future thinking,

00:04:30.948 --> 00:04:33.146
and that future starts to pull them

00:04:33.146 --> 00:04:35.229
towards those objectives.

00:04:37.028 --> 00:04:40.624
So I set my goals pretty
high, and I set my calendar

00:04:40.624 --> 00:04:42.978
far in advance, I'm planning,

00:04:42.978 --> 00:04:45.705
I still have some spontaneity,
room for spontaneity,

00:04:45.705 --> 00:04:49.288
but more and more as
the demands on my time

00:04:52.348 --> 00:04:56.644
are growing exponentially, I have to plan.

00:04:56.644 --> 00:05:00.811
And what I've, I've done
this for, gosh, 25 years,

00:05:02.184 --> 00:05:04.517
so look back and look forward.

00:05:04.517 --> 00:05:07.107
Look back take inventory, be honest,

00:05:07.107 --> 00:05:09.604
and look forward and map it out.

00:05:09.604 --> 00:05:13.080
So I want you to think
about short term, mid term,

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:17.656
long term goals, for you
personally and for your team.

00:05:17.656 --> 00:05:21.823
Create an environment that
supports your goals, your dreams.

00:05:23.643 --> 00:05:25.043
What do I mean by that,

00:05:25.043 --> 00:05:27.886
make sure the people
around you are pushing you

00:05:27.886 --> 00:05:30.433
in the direction of your dreams,
not patting you on the back

00:05:30.433 --> 00:05:33.122
for doing less than you're
capable, but pushing you

00:05:33.122 --> 00:05:34.345
to do more.

00:05:34.345 --> 00:05:36.817
Make sure the things
you're feeding your mind

00:05:36.817 --> 00:05:38.574
are pushing you in the
direction of your dreams.

00:05:38.574 --> 00:05:41.069
Make sure that you're
protecting your mind from things

00:05:41.069 --> 00:05:44.436
that would distract you from your dreams.

00:05:44.436 --> 00:05:47.667
It's your job, it's your
job, to create a bubble,

00:05:47.667 --> 00:05:51.115
to create an environment,
to create this ecosystem

00:05:51.115 --> 00:05:53.532
that will support your goals.

00:05:54.710 --> 00:05:56.907
Because if you're surrounded by people

00:05:56.907 --> 00:05:59.220
that are constantly distracting you,

00:05:59.220 --> 00:06:00.962
it's going to be very
difficult for you to grow

00:06:00.962 --> 00:06:02.090
a network marketing business.

00:06:02.090 --> 00:06:04.017
If you're surrounded by
people who are patting you

00:06:04.017 --> 00:06:06.686
on the back for doing one
tenth of what you're capable of

00:06:06.686 --> 00:06:08.901
instead of pushing you and challenging you

00:06:08.901 --> 00:06:10.936
and getting in your face,

00:06:10.936 --> 00:06:13.330
then there's only so far you can go.

00:06:13.330 --> 00:06:15.997
If you're constantly feeding
your mind and allowing

00:06:15.997 --> 00:06:19.579
your mind to be infected
by negative pessimistic

00:06:19.579 --> 00:06:23.583
compromising thoughts, then you can guess

00:06:23.583 --> 00:06:25.801
what your results are going to be.

00:06:25.801 --> 00:06:27.193
So guess who's job, it's not,

00:06:27.193 --> 00:06:30.077
you're not trying to
look for an environment

00:06:30.077 --> 00:06:31.124
that will support you,

00:06:31.124 --> 00:06:35.488
your job is to create an
environment that will support you.

00:06:35.488 --> 00:06:39.958
Create this community
around you, create the right

00:06:39.958 --> 00:06:41.642
friendships, the right mentoring,

00:06:41.642 --> 00:06:44.135
the right coaching, the right ideas,

00:06:44.135 --> 00:06:46.953
the right encouragement,
the right challenge,

00:06:46.953 --> 00:06:49.257
for you to be able to
go where you need to go.

00:06:49.257 --> 00:06:50.927
You understand what I'm saying?

00:06:50.927 --> 00:06:55.094
So, it's your job to hold
yourself accountable and create

00:06:55.962 --> 00:07:00.863
systems to hold yourself
accountable to a higher standard.

00:07:00.863 --> 00:07:03.372
Your dreams are worth it, I promise.

00:07:03.372 --> 00:07:04.753
If you're frustrated
and you don't know why

00:07:04.753 --> 00:07:08.290
you can't take action,
this is the big reason why.

00:07:08.290 --> 00:07:11.906
You can't seem to get
things going, this is why.

00:07:11.906 --> 00:07:15.792
So one, determine those
dreams, get 'em lock solid.

00:07:15.792 --> 00:07:18.119
Two, hold yourself
accountable towards 'em.

00:07:18.119 --> 00:07:21.331
And three, create a system around you

00:07:21.331 --> 00:07:23.450
of people and influences around you,

00:07:23.450 --> 00:07:26.231
that will challenge
you, that will push you,

00:07:26.231 --> 00:07:30.398
that will force you sometimes
to do the things necessary

00:07:31.797 --> 00:07:34.166
to make your dreams a reality.

00:07:34.166 --> 00:07:38.161
I've had to evolve so many
times, I've had to change

00:07:38.161 --> 00:07:40.673
and grow so many times.

00:07:40.673 --> 00:07:43.793
There's been times when
I've made such huge mistakes

00:07:43.793 --> 00:07:45.595
in my network marketing career.

00:07:45.595 --> 00:07:48.284
Damaged relationships, done
things that I wish I could

00:07:48.284 --> 00:07:50.679
go back and change, but I couldn't.

00:07:50.679 --> 00:07:53.878
So I could either live
there, or I could use that

00:07:53.878 --> 00:07:57.210
information to grow and become better.

00:07:57.210 --> 00:08:00.542
See I've been involved for
25 years and I promise you,

00:08:00.542 --> 00:08:03.057
every year that you, that we're engaged,

00:08:03.057 --> 00:08:05.933
we're working together, every
year you're going to see me

00:08:05.933 --> 00:08:08.319
get a little bit better,
get a little bit better,

00:08:08.319 --> 00:08:10.496
and most of the time I'm
not going to hit my goals,

00:08:10.496 --> 00:08:12.056
but then I'm going to
get a little bit better,

00:08:12.056 --> 00:08:15.230
and a little bit better,
and compounded over time,

00:08:15.230 --> 00:08:16.590
you'll see noticeable results.

00:08:16.590 --> 00:08:18.269
Anybody who knows me knows
that I'm a different person

00:08:18.269 --> 00:08:20.807
than I was five years ago, 10 years ago,

00:08:20.807 --> 00:08:23.504
15 years ago, certainly 25 years ago.

00:08:23.504 --> 00:08:26.660
18 jobs, you know, barely surviving,

00:08:26.660 --> 00:08:28.693
so give yourself some grace.

00:08:28.693 --> 00:08:32.032
Understand that nothing is ever finished

00:08:32.032 --> 00:08:33.908
while you're still alive.

00:08:33.908 --> 00:08:36.503
But here's what I believe
is the most powerful force,

00:08:36.503 --> 00:08:38.882
one of the most powerful forces on earth,

00:08:38.882 --> 00:08:41.873
and that is your imagination.

00:08:41.873 --> 00:08:43.774
What you can imagine.

00:08:43.774 --> 00:08:46.801
Now most people misuse their imagination,

00:08:46.801 --> 00:08:48.129
in other words, they think about

00:08:48.129 --> 00:08:49.881
what bad things could happen.

00:08:49.881 --> 00:08:53.946
They let their imagination
go wild to the negative side.

00:08:53.946 --> 00:08:56.074
How they could get hurt,
how they could get rejected,

00:08:56.074 --> 00:08:57.910
what could, you know,
all the terrible things

00:08:57.910 --> 00:08:59.410
that could happen.

00:09:00.735 --> 00:09:04.808
But the most successful
people, and I will tell ya

00:09:04.808 --> 00:09:07.996
I've used this in my life
for my whole life and it's,

00:09:07.996 --> 00:09:10.702
well my whole adult career at least,

00:09:10.702 --> 00:09:12.542
and it's worked unbelievable,

00:09:12.542 --> 00:09:16.055
is using your imagination for good.

00:09:16.055 --> 00:09:18.098
Using it for growth.

00:09:18.098 --> 00:09:20.681
Now here's what I mean by that.

00:09:21.602 --> 00:09:23.126
If you pick a goal, whatever it is,

00:09:23.126 --> 00:09:24.780
let's say you want to
meet someone, let's say

00:09:24.780 --> 00:09:26.964
you want to achieve a rank,
let's say you want to get

00:09:26.964 --> 00:09:30.609
to an income goal, let's say
you want to have a certain

00:09:30.609 --> 00:09:33.789
number of people in your group
at the next company event,

00:09:33.789 --> 00:09:35.980
whatever it is, okay?

00:09:35.980 --> 00:09:40.465
I want you to clearly
imagine it, get it so clear

00:09:40.465 --> 00:09:45.005
in your mind that it's like
you're living it in reality.

00:09:45.005 --> 00:09:47.234
What does it look like,
what does it feel like,

00:09:47.234 --> 00:09:50.032
what does it smell like,
what does it taste like,

00:09:50.032 --> 00:09:52.127
as clear as you can get it.

00:09:52.127 --> 00:09:56.731
And when you're talking
about what this picture

00:09:56.731 --> 00:09:57.968
in your mind,

00:09:57.968 --> 00:10:00.441
it's good to put it in
writing, and it's good

00:10:00.441 --> 00:10:04.252
to make it as detailed
as you possibly can.

00:10:04.252 --> 00:10:07.082
How do you feel now that
you've achieved that goal?

00:10:07.082 --> 00:10:09.672
How many lives are you
impacting now that you've

00:10:09.672 --> 00:10:12.322
accomplished that
objective, whatever it is,

00:10:12.322 --> 00:10:13.864
doesn't matter what it is.

00:10:13.864 --> 00:10:17.531
But the key is detail,
the key is specifics.

00:10:19.055 --> 00:10:23.138
The key is a clear, crystal
clear mental picture.

00:10:25.312 --> 00:10:29.227
So get it clear, and then
just go about your life,

00:10:29.227 --> 00:10:33.012
but here's, what ends up
happening and it's happened

00:10:33.012 --> 00:10:36.408
to me so many times
you can't even imagine,

00:10:36.408 --> 00:10:38.492
as soon as I get it clearly in my mind,

00:10:38.492 --> 00:10:41.626
it's not long before that
thing becomes a reality.

00:10:41.626 --> 00:10:44.960
Now it's not a magic trick, okay?

00:10:44.960 --> 00:10:48.261
You can't just sit at home
and imagine a Lamborghini

00:10:48.261 --> 00:10:49.898
and it pulls up into the
driveway and somebody

00:10:49.898 --> 00:10:51.156
gives you the keys,

00:10:51.156 --> 00:10:54.674
it's not a magic trick like that.

00:10:54.674 --> 00:10:57.565
Here's why I believe it works.

00:10:57.565 --> 00:11:01.251
Your subconscious brain
is working all the time,

00:11:01.251 --> 00:11:02.688
no matter what you're doing.

00:11:02.688 --> 00:11:06.241
It's working, it's helping
you guide and shift

00:11:06.241 --> 00:11:08.320
and make different decisions,

00:11:08.320 --> 00:11:10.742
but if you get a clear
picture in your mind,

00:11:10.742 --> 00:11:14.909
I believe you unlock the power
of your subconscious mind.

00:11:17.157 --> 00:11:19.947
And when you unlock the power
of your subconscious mind,

00:11:19.947 --> 00:11:23.734
it starts to grind and
grind and grind and grind,

00:11:23.734 --> 00:11:25.109
to make the picture that you have

00:11:25.109 --> 00:11:27.808
in your imagination a reality.

00:11:27.808 --> 00:11:30.836
And there starts to be
thousands of what I like to call

00:11:30.836 --> 00:11:34.387
micro-decisions that start to happen.

00:11:34.387 --> 00:11:37.101
Little left turn right turn,
little course corrections,

00:11:37.101 --> 00:11:41.000
thousands of them, that
are happening all the time.

00:11:41.000 --> 00:11:44.819
While you sleep, your
subconscious brain is working

00:11:44.819 --> 00:11:48.938
to help guide you towards that objective.

00:11:48.938 --> 00:11:50.908
If you're mowing the lawn,
if you're doing the laundry,

00:11:50.908 --> 00:11:53.839
that subconscious mind is
working, if your imagination

00:11:53.839 --> 00:11:57.067
is strong enough and clear
enough, your subconscious mind

00:11:57.067 --> 00:12:00.362
is working and working and
grinding and grinding and moving,

00:12:00.362 --> 00:12:02.769
it's not like you're
attracting those things to you,

00:12:02.769 --> 00:12:04.864
you're attracting yourself to those things

00:12:04.864 --> 00:12:09.593
because your subconscious
mind is working for you.

00:12:09.593 --> 00:12:13.201
It's like a slave for you,
working and grinding and working

00:12:13.201 --> 00:12:15.170
and grinding and working and grinding

00:12:15.170 --> 00:12:17.467
to help you get to your objective.

00:12:17.467 --> 00:12:19.306
Thousands and thousands
of little decisions

00:12:19.306 --> 00:12:22.309
you didn't even know why you
made them, they were made

00:12:22.309 --> 00:12:26.063
because one, you had a
clear picture in your mind.

00:12:26.063 --> 00:12:28.898
Two, your subconscious brain went to work

00:12:28.898 --> 00:12:31.107
without you even realizing it.

00:12:31.107 --> 00:12:35.015
And three, step by step, inch
by inch, you moved closer

00:12:35.015 --> 00:12:38.385
to your objective until you attained it.

00:12:38.385 --> 00:12:40.039
So the picture that you have in your mind

00:12:40.039 --> 00:12:42.537
is incredibly important
because guess what,

00:12:42.537 --> 00:12:44.797
if you have negative picture in your mind,

00:12:44.797 --> 00:12:47.381
a negative picture in your imagination,

00:12:47.381 --> 00:12:49.113
your subconscious mind's
going to go to work

00:12:49.113 --> 00:12:51.910
to make that a reality too.

00:12:51.910 --> 00:12:54.433
Thousands of little
micro-decisions to guide you

00:12:54.433 --> 00:12:56.296
towards the negative.

00:12:56.296 --> 00:12:58.786
So, who wants to live with that?

00:12:58.786 --> 00:13:01.361
Who wants to put your
subconscious mind to work

00:13:01.361 --> 00:13:05.588
as your employee to work for
you and work against you?

00:13:05.588 --> 00:13:07.529
Why would you want to do that?

00:13:07.529 --> 00:13:10.613
So get a clear picture of your
goals, of your objectives,

00:13:10.613 --> 00:13:13.372
of your vision of anything
you want to accomplish,

00:13:13.372 --> 00:13:16.572
anyone that you want to meet,
anything that you want to do.

00:13:16.572 --> 00:13:18.607
I've envisioned getting on a stage

00:13:18.607 --> 00:13:20.039
that I wanted to speak on.

00:13:20.039 --> 00:13:23.813
I've envisioned having
thousands of people in the room.

00:13:23.813 --> 00:13:26.628
I've envisioned relationships
with top of my heroes

00:13:26.628 --> 00:13:28.181
of personal development, with Jim Rohn's

00:13:28.181 --> 00:13:30.640
and the Tony Robbin's,
and the Richard Branson's

00:13:30.640 --> 00:13:32.009
and all the different people.

00:13:32.009 --> 00:13:33.409
I've imagined those relationships

00:13:33.409 --> 00:13:36.824
long before they became a reality.

00:13:36.824 --> 00:13:39.321
And then my subconscious
mind went to work.

00:13:39.321 --> 00:13:43.166
And it ground, it was grinding
and grinding and grinding

00:13:43.166 --> 00:13:45.154
and grinding, thousands of decisions

00:13:45.154 --> 00:13:47.654
until it became a reality.

00:13:47.654 --> 00:13:49.712
So one, think of something
that's important to you,

00:13:49.712 --> 00:13:52.446
get it clear in your mind,
and then let your subconscious

00:13:52.446 --> 00:13:55.415
mind grind for you, let it work for you,

00:13:55.415 --> 00:13:58.378
let it create results for you.

00:13:58.378 --> 00:14:00.968
In this book, the one that I was just

00:14:00.968 --> 00:14:02.931
reading over the weekend,

00:14:02.931 --> 00:14:05.083
he talks about the fact
that you know what,

00:14:05.083 --> 00:14:08.413
if times are bad for you right now,

00:14:08.413 --> 00:14:11.883
if the wind is blowing
in your face right now,

00:14:11.883 --> 00:14:16.417
just hang in there because
the wind can change.

00:14:16.417 --> 00:14:18.812
The wind will change, and
if the wind's in your face,

00:14:18.812 --> 00:14:22.322
the wind can change and be
on your, be at your back

00:14:22.322 --> 00:14:25.497
and propel you forward
and I really struggled

00:14:25.497 --> 00:14:29.855
with this message, I really
had a difficult time with it

00:14:29.855 --> 00:14:32.584
because I've listened
to so much of Jim Rohn,

00:14:32.584 --> 00:14:35.917
and because if you know anything at all,

00:14:37.009 --> 00:14:38.399
which I'm an amateur,
but if you know anything

00:14:38.399 --> 00:14:40.149
at all about sailing,

00:14:42.965 --> 00:14:44.963
it doesn't matter what the wind is doing,

00:14:44.963 --> 00:14:47.816
if it's at your back or
if it's in your face,

00:14:47.816 --> 00:14:51.240
there is a way for you to move forward.

00:14:51.240 --> 00:14:53.117
If the wind is in your face
and you have a sail boat,

00:14:53.117 --> 00:14:56.266
you just go back and
forth and back and forth,

00:14:56.266 --> 00:14:59.433
using that same wind to go forward.

00:14:59.433 --> 00:15:01.685
I will tell you, there's a group of people

00:15:01.685 --> 00:15:03.928
who are crossing their fingers today

00:15:03.928 --> 00:15:07.573
and they're waiting
for the wind to change.

00:15:07.573 --> 00:15:10.740
There's a group of people
who are hoping and praying

00:15:10.740 --> 00:15:14.911
that the wind changes, and
what I want to tell all of you,

00:15:14.911 --> 00:15:18.101
if you're, if any of those people are you,

00:15:18.101 --> 00:15:21.644
is you don't need to wait
for the wind to change.

00:15:21.644 --> 00:15:25.811
The wind, whichever way it
blows, can be your friend.

00:15:27.875 --> 00:15:30.336
If it's in your face, you
have a different approach

00:15:30.336 --> 00:15:32.006
to how you move forward.

00:15:32.006 --> 00:15:34.108
If it's from the side, you
have a different approach

00:15:34.108 --> 00:15:35.145
to how you move forward.

00:15:35.145 --> 00:15:37.225
If it's at your back, there's
going to be times when it's

00:15:37.225 --> 00:15:41.095
at your back, sure, everybody
can move forward quickly

00:15:41.095 --> 00:15:43.654
when the wind's at your back.

00:15:43.654 --> 00:15:47.623
But when it's not, and
it's not most of the time,

00:15:47.623 --> 00:15:49.862
you have to have a
strategy to move forward.

00:15:49.862 --> 00:15:52.413
We can change the sail and we can have

00:15:52.413 --> 00:15:55.114
total control regardless of the wind.

00:15:55.114 --> 00:15:58.064
We can decide which
direction we're going to go

00:15:58.064 --> 00:15:59.699
regardless of the wind.

00:15:59.699 --> 00:16:03.186
We don't have to wait
for something out there

00:16:03.186 --> 00:16:06.269
to happen in order for us to be okay.

00:16:07.259 --> 00:16:10.692
It's not out there ladies
and gentlemen, it's in here.

00:16:10.692 --> 00:16:13.442
It's not out there, it's in here.

00:16:14.641 --> 00:16:18.344
So not only do you need to
take charge when it comes

00:16:18.344 --> 00:16:20.999
to setting the sail of your life,

00:16:20.999 --> 00:16:24.992
we need to let the whole
world know, while they're all

00:16:24.992 --> 00:16:28.044
waiting for this wind to
change, and it might and it may

00:16:28.044 --> 00:16:31.856
change, but of course at some
point it's going to change,

00:16:31.856 --> 00:16:36.452
but it may not change for
some people for a long time.

00:16:36.452 --> 00:16:41.394
We can give them an opportunity
and the skills to be able

00:16:41.394 --> 00:16:45.561
to prosper regardless of
the direction of the wind.

00:16:47.264 --> 00:16:49.744
Do you get what I'm saying to you?

00:16:49.744 --> 00:16:51.972
It's not out there ladies and gentlemen,

00:16:51.972 --> 00:16:53.659
it's right in here.

00:16:53.659 --> 00:16:56.397
Once you get that, you realize
how much power you actually

00:16:56.397 --> 00:17:00.525
really have in controlling
the direction of your life,

00:17:00.525 --> 00:17:02.279
everything'll change for you.

00:17:02.279 --> 00:17:06.275
Instead of focusing just on
the how, one of the skills,

00:17:06.275 --> 00:17:09.488
not only just the tactical
skills of how to do things,

00:17:09.488 --> 00:17:13.218
but the skills of
understanding the human element

00:17:13.218 --> 00:17:15.575
of what it is that we do.

00:17:15.575 --> 00:17:19.934
If you know why you need to
use your own product or service

00:17:19.934 --> 00:17:24.101
every single day, then it's
easy to develop structures

00:17:25.495 --> 00:17:27.960
for everybody to learn how to do that.

00:17:27.960 --> 00:17:30.241
If you know why it's
important to build your story,

00:17:30.241 --> 00:17:32.518
if you know why it's important
to go to your events,

00:17:32.518 --> 00:17:36.717
if you know why it's important
to share the opportunity,

00:17:36.717 --> 00:17:41.567
if you know why it's important
to utilize third party tools,

00:17:41.567 --> 00:17:44.065
if you know why it's important to

00:17:44.065 --> 00:17:46.126
be able to give a strong testimonial,

00:17:46.126 --> 00:17:49.406
if you know why it's important to focus on

00:17:49.406 --> 00:17:53.390
personal development,
then the how to gets easy,

00:17:53.390 --> 00:17:57.101
and if you know why, and you
get that why strong enough,

00:17:57.101 --> 00:17:59.990
you can help all those
people that have been

00:17:59.990 --> 00:18:04.424
in assignment oriented
living for their whole life,

00:18:04.424 --> 00:18:05.308
in other words they've been doing

00:18:05.308 --> 00:18:07.157
what they're told their whole life,

00:18:07.157 --> 00:18:09.842
a lot of people are waiting
for somebody like you

00:18:09.842 --> 00:18:13.520
who understands why it
is that we do what we do,

00:18:13.520 --> 00:18:17.378
to be able to inspire those
people to start to do it,

00:18:17.378 --> 00:18:19.588
to do the how to, and then eventually

00:18:19.588 --> 00:18:21.267
they'll develop the why to.

00:18:21.267 --> 00:18:25.401
Once I understood this concept of the why,

00:18:25.401 --> 00:18:27.034
the person who knows how to
do something will always work

00:18:27.034 --> 00:18:28.410
for the person who knows why to something,

00:18:28.410 --> 00:18:30.806
well I don't want to work for
anybody the rest of my life.

00:18:30.806 --> 00:18:33.220
What I want to do is I want to focus on

00:18:33.220 --> 00:18:34.873
why am I doing everything?

00:18:34.873 --> 00:18:37.778
Why does this work in network marketing,

00:18:37.778 --> 00:18:39.940
why does this not work
in network marketing?

00:18:39.940 --> 00:18:44.107
I understood all of the
mechanical, psychological triggers

00:18:45.401 --> 00:18:47.803
that made our business
work, and once I understood

00:18:47.803 --> 00:18:51.507
the why's not only did
the how's get easy for me,

00:18:51.507 --> 00:18:53.523
but it became very easy for me to inspire

00:18:53.523 --> 00:18:55.632
other people to take action.

00:18:55.632 --> 00:18:58.371
Because I understood the true
reasons why to do something,

00:18:58.371 --> 00:19:00.724
I wasn't just saying
do it 'cause I said so.

00:19:00.724 --> 00:19:03.821
I could explain that philosophy to them.

00:19:03.821 --> 00:19:07.934
I switched my mind from
becoming the best how to guy

00:19:07.934 --> 00:19:10.479
that you would ever meet,
to becoming the best

00:19:10.479 --> 00:19:13.150
why to guy that you'll ever meet.

00:19:13.150 --> 00:19:15.098
Changed my business, changed my life.

00:19:15.098 --> 00:19:17.792
I will tell you, if you
implement this in your business,

00:19:17.792 --> 00:19:18.955
it'll change yours too.

00:19:18.955 --> 00:19:21.788
You can't afford to mow your lawn,

00:19:23.116 --> 00:19:25.008
what does that title even mean?

00:19:25.008 --> 00:19:28.524
Let me back up and give
you some context to it,

00:19:28.524 --> 00:19:30.529
and I think by the end of this show,

00:19:30.529 --> 00:19:32.278
you're going to agree with me.

00:19:32.278 --> 00:19:33.881
If you're involved in network marketing,

00:19:33.881 --> 00:19:35.183
if you're an entrepreneur,

00:19:35.183 --> 00:19:37.524
you can't afford to mow your lawn.

00:19:37.524 --> 00:19:40.544
Now here's where this all started for me.

00:19:40.544 --> 00:19:43.348
I've been mentored by a
few different billionaires

00:19:43.348 --> 00:19:45.989
over the course of my career.

00:19:45.989 --> 00:19:50.380
And the first one, I
went to him and I said,

00:19:50.380 --> 00:19:53.411
"You know, I want to achieve,
I want to move forward,

00:19:53.411 --> 00:19:56.567
"you've had all this
success, what do I do,

00:19:56.567 --> 00:19:59.058
"how do I break out, how do I create

00:19:59.058 --> 00:20:00.545
"more success for myself?"

00:20:00.545 --> 00:20:03.985
He said, "Eric, how much do
you want to make in a year,

00:20:03.985 --> 00:20:05.464
"give me a number."

00:20:05.464 --> 00:20:08.754
I said, "Well, a million
a year sounds good,

00:20:08.754 --> 00:20:11.110
"you know, two commas, a
million dollars a year.

00:20:11.110 --> 00:20:15.171
"That sounds like it would
be, you know, a great life."

00:20:15.171 --> 00:20:16.119
He said, "Fine,"

00:20:16.119 --> 00:20:17.424
he said, "That's a good start.

00:20:17.424 --> 00:20:19.512
"Let's break that down.

00:20:19.512 --> 00:20:21.265
"To make a million dollars a year,

00:20:21.265 --> 00:20:25.432
"you would have to earn
approximately $500 an hour

00:20:26.961 --> 00:20:29.020
"in your work time.

00:20:29.020 --> 00:20:33.798
"$500 an hour in your work time,
in order to be able to earn

00:20:33.798 --> 00:20:35.255
"a million dollars a year."

00:20:35.255 --> 00:20:39.831
He said, "Eric, is there
a task that you can do

00:20:39.831 --> 00:20:43.599
"in your business, that will earn you

00:20:43.599 --> 00:20:45.682
"$500 an hour over time."

00:20:47.185 --> 00:20:51.779
I went, "Well, in network
marketing, there actually is."

00:20:51.779 --> 00:20:55.684
If I'm in front of a prospect,
if I'm tellin' the story,

00:20:55.684 --> 00:20:57.523
if I'm sharin' the product,
I'm tellin' the story,

00:20:57.523 --> 00:20:59.325
I'm sharing the
opportunity, I'm explaining

00:20:59.325 --> 00:21:01.936
the compensation plan,
I'm with a prospect,

00:21:01.936 --> 00:21:05.217
helping them understand what
it is that I have to offer,

00:21:05.217 --> 00:21:09.461
if I'm with that prospect, that over time,

00:21:09.461 --> 00:21:11.961
equals $500 an hour or better.

00:21:13.326 --> 00:21:15.918
That was my experience.

00:21:15.918 --> 00:21:18.031
I just didn't spend that much time

00:21:18.031 --> 00:21:19.816
in front of that many prospects, right?

00:21:19.816 --> 00:21:23.988
I would, I'd get, my life was
busy with everything else.

00:21:23.988 --> 00:21:28.848
I said, "Yeah," I said,
"Yes, I have that activity."

00:21:28.848 --> 00:21:29.921
He said, "Fine."

00:21:29.921 --> 00:21:34.004
He said, "take every
activity that you are doing,

00:21:35.935 --> 00:21:40.193
"that's, that you, that can
be done by someone else,

00:21:40.193 --> 00:21:43.851
"number one, the activity that
can be done by someone else,

00:21:43.851 --> 00:21:48.018
"number one, number two, is
worth less than $500 an hour,

00:21:51.238 --> 00:21:53.199
"and number three, isn't something

00:21:53.199 --> 00:21:57.016
"that's jeapordizing your
family or your values,

00:21:57.016 --> 00:22:00.416
"and have somebody else do it."

00:22:00.416 --> 00:22:04.040
So, I said, "So, wait a
minute, so, I mow my lawn,

00:22:04.040 --> 00:22:06.044
"you're telling me I can't mow my lawn?"

00:22:06.044 --> 00:22:08.330
He said, "You can mow your
lawn, but mowing your lawn

00:22:08.330 --> 00:22:11.198
"is minimum wage activity.

00:22:11.198 --> 00:22:15.198
"If you want to sell your
hour for minimum wage,

00:22:16.342 --> 00:22:18.910
"and there's a task you
could do somewhere else

00:22:18.910 --> 00:22:23.077
"that's paying $500 an
hour, why would you do that?

00:22:23.994 --> 00:22:27.541
"Call it $15 an hour to mow your lawn,

00:22:27.541 --> 00:22:30.045
"and you have a task
that you could get $500

00:22:30.045 --> 00:22:31.662
"if you're in front of prospects?

00:22:31.662 --> 00:22:35.495
"Every time you mow your
lawn, you lose $485."

00:22:37.811 --> 00:22:39.228
And I went, "Wow.

00:22:40.193 --> 00:22:42.735
"I thought I was saving
money by mowing my lawn."

00:22:42.735 --> 00:22:46.318
No, it was costing me
money to mow my lawn.

00:22:47.971 --> 00:22:49.529
So here's what I did.

00:22:49.529 --> 00:22:52.094
I took inventory of every part of my life.

00:22:52.094 --> 00:22:56.261
I currently, and for decades
now, have not done tasks

00:22:59.235 --> 00:23:02.721
of under $500 an hour, unless it was

00:23:02.721 --> 00:23:03.862
something with my family,

00:23:03.862 --> 00:23:05.730
unless it was something that I chose to do

00:23:05.730 --> 00:23:08.201
that was quality with the
relationships in my life,

00:23:08.201 --> 00:23:11.113
I'm talking about work time,
I'm talking about time,

00:23:11.113 --> 00:23:12.972
think tasks that I could do,

00:23:12.972 --> 00:23:16.807
that don't impact my relationships, okay?

00:23:16.807 --> 00:23:19.620
So, I don't mow the lawn.

00:23:19.620 --> 00:23:21.613
I don't clean the pool.

00:23:21.613 --> 00:23:24.729
I don't clean out the garage.

00:23:24.729 --> 00:23:26.562
I don't get groceries.

00:23:27.729 --> 00:23:29.729
I don't clean the house.

00:23:30.903 --> 00:23:33.836
I don't do any of that stuff.

00:23:33.836 --> 00:23:38.227
In our family we have people
help us do those things,

00:23:38.227 --> 00:23:41.560
and then we focus our tasks, our energy,

00:23:42.665 --> 00:23:45.462
on the highest producing
activity possible.

00:23:45.462 --> 00:23:48.211
Mastering your emotions,
and people ask me sometimes,

00:23:48.211 --> 00:23:51.949
like, are emotions
important for entrepreneur?

00:23:51.949 --> 00:23:54.031
Managing emotions, does that important,

00:23:54.031 --> 00:23:57.158
seems like it would be all
discipline and hard work.

00:23:57.158 --> 00:23:59.975
Well guess what will cause
you to stay disciplined,

00:23:59.975 --> 00:24:01.688
and will cause you to do the hard work,

00:24:01.688 --> 00:24:04.002
is mastering your emotions.

00:24:04.002 --> 00:24:08.134
Trying to figure out that the
triggers that cause you to act

00:24:08.134 --> 00:24:10.051
or cause you to freeze,

00:24:10.887 --> 00:24:14.315
and one of the most interesting
concepts, and I learned

00:24:14.315 --> 00:24:17.956
this from Tony Robbins, he and
I were talking this last year

00:24:17.956 --> 00:24:22.196
several times about this
concept, it's so interesting,

00:24:22.196 --> 00:24:25.696
and that is, what is your default emotion?

00:24:26.844 --> 00:24:29.016
In other words, when poked, when prodded,

00:24:29.016 --> 00:24:33.183
when bored, when either
stimulated or not stimulated,

00:24:35.784 --> 00:24:39.288
what emotion is your go to emotion?

00:24:39.288 --> 00:24:42.224
Now, for some people, it's stress.

00:24:42.224 --> 00:24:44.758
Entrepreneurs, a lot of
entrepreneurs like to go,

00:24:44.758 --> 00:24:46.411
"I'm stressed out, I'm
just stressed right now."

00:24:46.411 --> 00:24:48.572
That's their go to emotion.

00:24:48.572 --> 00:24:52.739
They go into their mind and
that is, that's what they go to

00:24:53.699 --> 00:24:55.200
as a default.

00:24:55.200 --> 00:24:57.504
That's their neutral, okay?

00:24:57.504 --> 00:25:01.671
Some people, use worry to
worry about something that

00:25:02.947 --> 00:25:05.785
might happen, worry about what
somebody else might think,

00:25:05.785 --> 00:25:10.434
worry about some circumstance
outside of their control.

00:25:10.434 --> 00:25:12.439
Worry about what's going
on with their comp plan,

00:25:12.439 --> 00:25:13.984
or worry about what's
happening with the product,

00:25:13.984 --> 00:25:15.281
or worrying about what's going on

00:25:15.281 --> 00:25:16.416
with the international expansion,

00:25:16.416 --> 00:25:18.795
or worrying about decisions
the team is making,

00:25:18.795 --> 00:25:20.168
or the company is making, or worrying

00:25:20.168 --> 00:25:23.213
about an event that's
coming up, or something,

00:25:23.213 --> 00:25:25.493
that's their default emotion.

00:25:25.493 --> 00:25:29.413
Some people it's to fight,
their default emotion is anger.

00:25:29.413 --> 00:25:32.102
They want to fight, they're
looking for an enemy all the time.

00:25:32.102 --> 00:25:34.988
That's their default emotion, okay?

00:25:34.988 --> 00:25:38.182
So we all have a choice,
and we all have to decide

00:25:38.182 --> 00:25:41.346
what is the default emotion
that's going to serve us,

00:25:41.346 --> 00:25:43.589
and is the current one
that we have the one

00:25:43.589 --> 00:25:45.657
that's serving us the most?

00:25:45.657 --> 00:25:48.224
Because if it's on the negative side,

00:25:48.224 --> 00:25:51.641
stress, frustration, doubt, worry, anger,

00:25:54.405 --> 00:25:58.580
all of those, which
many entrepreneurs have,

00:25:58.580 --> 00:26:02.747
if we, if our default is
there, inside of that space,

00:26:03.911 --> 00:26:07.661
it's like putting a
limiter on our potential.

00:26:09.967 --> 00:26:11.429
When we're in that space,
do you think we are

00:26:11.429 --> 00:26:14.972
attracting people to us, or do you think

00:26:14.972 --> 00:26:17.192
we may be pushing some people away?

00:26:17.192 --> 00:26:19.571
Are we making people want
to be around us a lot,

00:26:19.571 --> 00:26:22.859
are we maybe only attracting
other angry people,

00:26:22.859 --> 00:26:26.869
or other stressed out people
that we can relate to?

00:26:26.869 --> 00:26:28.619
So, there's a choice.

00:26:29.648 --> 00:26:31.913
There's another range of emotions,

00:26:31.913 --> 00:26:35.606
now that doesn't mean you
can't bounce into stress,

00:26:35.606 --> 00:26:38.852
which is just fear, you
can't bounce into anger,

00:26:38.852 --> 00:26:41.852
or defending somebody, or something,

00:26:42.735 --> 00:26:47.657
you can't bounce into
frustration or worry or doubt,

00:26:47.657 --> 00:26:50.262
but what's the default,
where do you go back to?

00:26:50.262 --> 00:26:53.845
What's center, what is neutral for you?

00:26:53.845 --> 00:26:58.012
And, for me, it was an
interesting exercise to kind of

00:26:58.883 --> 00:27:01.517
go through this, as like wow,
because when I was talking

00:27:01.517 --> 00:27:05.706
with Tony about it, he was
saying that he has so much

00:27:05.706 --> 00:27:07.842
going on in his life, that it's very easy

00:27:07.842 --> 00:27:11.600
for stress to become he default emotion.

00:27:11.600 --> 00:27:15.923
So, he finally realized
that no, no that's a choice.

00:27:15.923 --> 00:27:17.675
I could choose to look at something,

00:27:17.675 --> 00:27:20.280
anything part of my life
and get stressed about it,

00:27:20.280 --> 00:27:23.384
but my default emotion, could I replace

00:27:23.384 --> 00:27:26.747
that default emotion for passion?

00:27:26.747 --> 00:27:29.914
For joy, for happiness, for gratitude?

00:27:32.221 --> 00:27:34.712
Those default emotions.

00:27:34.712 --> 00:27:37.994
What if your default emotion
was gratitude, all the time?

00:27:37.994 --> 00:27:39.595
What if it was joy all the time?

00:27:39.595 --> 00:27:41.462
Now you might get pushed and
get stressed out for a minute,

00:27:41.462 --> 00:27:44.888
but you come back to joy,
you come back to gratitude.

00:27:44.888 --> 00:27:47.174
You come back to happiness.

00:27:47.174 --> 00:27:48.007
Right?

00:27:48.007 --> 00:27:49.735
You come back to passion.

00:27:49.735 --> 00:27:53.847
And there's a difference
between passion and anger.

00:27:53.847 --> 00:27:58.014
If it's anger, that's going
to repel a lot of people.

00:27:58.865 --> 00:28:03.539
If it's passion, it's going
to attract tons of people

00:28:03.539 --> 00:28:06.062
into your life, into your world.

00:28:06.062 --> 00:28:09.325
So, I want you to think about
what your default emotion is,

00:28:09.325 --> 00:28:13.437
maybe even write down, what
is the emotion that you go to

00:28:13.437 --> 00:28:17.919
most when poked, when
something doesn't go perfect,

00:28:17.919 --> 00:28:22.002
when something unexpected
happens, when stressed.

00:28:22.939 --> 00:28:24.341
What is your default emotion, where do you

00:28:24.341 --> 00:28:26.583
go to there, okay?

00:28:26.583 --> 00:28:29.936
And just aside, that on the
other side of that coin,

00:28:29.936 --> 00:28:32.584
instead of expectation and anxiety,

00:28:32.584 --> 00:28:35.868
it can be appreciation and gratitude.

00:28:35.868 --> 00:28:39.701
Instead of anger, it can be passion.

00:28:39.701 --> 00:28:43.868
Instead of worry and doubt,
it can be joy and peace.

00:28:45.163 --> 00:28:47.468
That it's all going to be fine.

00:28:47.468 --> 00:28:49.135
So, we control this.

00:28:50.503 --> 00:28:52.405
We might not be able to control the pain,

00:28:52.405 --> 00:28:54.518
that we talk about this at
Go Pro Recruiting Mastery

00:28:54.518 --> 00:28:56.249
we talk about this more and more,

00:28:56.249 --> 00:28:58.643
we might not be able to
control physical pain,

00:28:58.643 --> 00:29:00.353
or mental emotional pain,

00:29:00.353 --> 00:29:04.320
but we can choose
suffering, that's a choice.

00:29:04.320 --> 00:29:05.245
The pain might not be a choice,

00:29:05.245 --> 00:29:07.692
but the, our emotional state is a choice.

00:29:07.692 --> 00:29:11.081
The one thing that Tony told
me that just knocked me down,

00:29:11.081 --> 00:29:15.248
is he and I both go up on stage
and we give a lot of energy

00:29:16.119 --> 00:29:18.048
and we're, you know,
we're very enthusiastic,

00:29:18.048 --> 00:29:19.701
we're very energetic,

00:29:19.701 --> 00:29:24.114
and then for me, when I get
off the stage, I like woo,

00:29:24.114 --> 00:29:27.809
I throttle back a bit,
I reset my batteries,

00:29:27.809 --> 00:29:31.976
so my stage energy is not my
default, it's an exception.

00:29:34.388 --> 00:29:37.457
So he told me, he said,
Eric, the biggest change

00:29:37.457 --> 00:29:41.755
to happen in his life, he
said to me, when we were

00:29:41.755 --> 00:29:43.285
doin' an interview this
last year, he said,

00:29:43.285 --> 00:29:45.349
"Eric the biggest change
to happen to me in my life

00:29:45.349 --> 00:29:48.836
"this last year, was I
decided to take the guy

00:29:48.836 --> 00:29:52.855
"that's on stage, I decided
to take him home with me.

00:29:52.855 --> 00:29:54.983
"And that was going to be my new default."

00:29:54.983 --> 00:29:57.111
And I went, "Wow, okay.

00:29:57.111 --> 00:29:59.517
That's something completely different."

00:29:59.517 --> 00:30:02.141
Think about you and your
best energetic state,

00:30:02.141 --> 00:30:06.110
your most attractive, your most outgoing,

00:30:06.110 --> 00:30:08.846
your most vibrant state possible,

00:30:08.846 --> 00:30:11.215
think about taking that
person home with you.

00:30:11.215 --> 00:30:13.200
Think about that being your new normal.

00:30:13.200 --> 00:30:17.367
Think about that being kind
of the, just a, every day,

00:30:18.733 --> 00:30:21.550
and the other negative stuff
is just kind of here and there,

00:30:21.550 --> 00:30:23.451
it just comes and it goes.

00:30:23.451 --> 00:30:25.975
But you have a different default state.

00:30:25.975 --> 00:30:27.623
Control that default state, you start

00:30:27.623 --> 00:30:30.087
to take control of your life.

00:30:30.087 --> 00:30:32.857
All entrepreneurs deal with
this issue of self-doubt,

00:30:32.857 --> 00:30:36.274
of challenge, of difficulty, of struggle.

00:30:37.235 --> 00:30:41.572
And, I don't know what
it is for you, I mean,

00:30:41.572 --> 00:30:44.139
for me I, so many things
went through my mind.

00:30:44.139 --> 00:30:45.908
Maybe this isn't for me.

00:30:45.908 --> 00:30:48.417
Maybe this just isn't my thing.

00:30:48.417 --> 00:30:51.635
Maybe other people are made
for this, maybe I'm not.

00:30:51.635 --> 00:30:55.247
Maybe entrepreneurs need to be born,

00:30:55.247 --> 00:30:56.919
'cause I wasn't born an entrepreneur,

00:30:56.919 --> 00:31:01.086
maybe I just need to be
realistic and just go get a job.

00:31:02.863 --> 00:31:06.186
Maybe I don't have the
discipline for this.

00:31:06.186 --> 00:31:08.767
Or some days when I would just
say, you know, I would get

00:31:08.767 --> 00:31:11.220
so discouraged with people,
because I couldn't get people

00:31:11.220 --> 00:31:13.589
to do the actions that
I was willing to do,

00:31:13.589 --> 00:31:16.064
maybe I'm just not a good enough leader.

00:31:16.064 --> 00:31:19.106
Maybe the product isn't,
you know, valuable enough.

00:31:19.106 --> 00:31:21.245
Maybe the compensation plan doesn't pay

00:31:21.245 --> 00:31:22.477
as much as I think it should.

00:31:22.477 --> 00:31:26.714
Maybe I'm in a country
or a part of the world

00:31:26.714 --> 00:31:29.970
that is, you know, I
feel is more resistant

00:31:29.970 --> 00:31:32.128
to network marketing than
any other part of the world,

00:31:32.128 --> 00:31:36.024
you know, so because of
that I'm going to struggle.

00:31:36.024 --> 00:31:39.524
Or whatever, there's, the list is so long,

00:31:40.804 --> 00:31:43.971
when it comes to reasons to check out.

00:31:46.744 --> 00:31:48.609
Reasons to walk away.

00:31:48.609 --> 00:31:50.895
You miss that rank,
you push for that goal,

00:31:50.895 --> 00:31:53.360
you get embarrassed, you fall on your face

00:31:53.360 --> 00:31:55.320
in front of your group, you try and do

00:31:55.320 --> 00:31:57.808
a presentation it doesn't go very well,

00:31:57.808 --> 00:32:00.716
you drive across town, you
go across the country even,

00:32:00.716 --> 00:32:04.184
to do a meeting and nobody shows up,

00:32:04.184 --> 00:32:06.974
somebody in your company
makes you feel bad

00:32:06.974 --> 00:32:09.152
or makes you feel small,
and because of that

00:32:09.152 --> 00:32:10.869
you get your feelings hurt.

00:32:10.869 --> 00:32:13.536
There's so many reasons to quit.

00:32:14.656 --> 00:32:17.864
And here's my message for you this week.

00:32:17.864 --> 00:32:22.031
If you're looking for a reason
to quit, they're all there.

00:32:23.474 --> 00:32:25.166
I just gave you a whole bunch of them.

00:32:25.166 --> 00:32:29.333
There's a whole menu of
reasons that you can choose,

00:32:30.306 --> 00:32:32.510
and no one will blame you.

00:32:32.510 --> 00:32:35.330
You can say hey, because of
this, I decided not to do it,

00:32:35.330 --> 00:32:38.391
and that makes you feel
better, and that explains it

00:32:38.391 --> 00:32:42.371
to the world, and you
move on with your life.

00:32:42.371 --> 00:32:45.549
There'll always be a reason to quit.

00:32:45.549 --> 00:32:48.805
But, if your dream is strong enough,

00:32:48.805 --> 00:32:52.181
there will always be a reason to stay.

00:32:52.181 --> 00:32:54.546
There will always be a
reason to push through.

00:32:54.546 --> 00:32:57.400
There will always be a
reason to help others.

00:32:57.400 --> 00:33:00.420
Maybe it's knowing that
your product or service

00:33:00.420 --> 00:33:03.288
is going to be, have
an impact on the world

00:33:03.288 --> 00:33:04.569
and you can't let that go.

00:33:04.569 --> 00:33:07.260
Or maybe it's you're rescuing
people from desperate lives,

00:33:07.260 --> 00:33:10.107
maybe it's taking care
of those family members

00:33:10.107 --> 00:33:12.777
that maybe can't take care of themselves

00:33:12.777 --> 00:33:15.638
as well as maybe you can help them do,

00:33:15.638 --> 00:33:17.947
maybe it's giving to the causes
that are important to you.

00:33:17.947 --> 00:33:20.687
Maybe it's seeing that
next person in your group,

00:33:20.687 --> 00:33:24.501
the fire light up in their
eyes, because of you,

00:33:24.501 --> 00:33:27.731
because you persevered, because you worked

00:33:27.731 --> 00:33:29.022
when no one else was watching,

00:33:29.022 --> 00:33:32.151
because you decided to do something

00:33:32.151 --> 00:33:35.301
that other people weren't willing to do.

00:33:35.301 --> 00:33:36.989
That sense of pride
that you did something,

00:33:36.989 --> 00:33:38.800
that sense of pride that
you went through the battle,

00:33:38.800 --> 00:33:42.800
the sense of pride that
you stood for something.

00:33:44.038 --> 00:33:46.107
That's more valuable in my opinion,

00:33:46.107 --> 00:33:48.961
than living a life full of regrets.

00:33:48.961 --> 00:33:51.054
Going through the challenge, understanding

00:33:51.054 --> 00:33:53.175
the challenge is what
makes something of you.

00:33:53.175 --> 00:33:57.045
The challenge is what
creates something of you.

00:33:57.045 --> 00:33:59.242
They say what doesn't kill
you makes you stronger,

00:33:59.242 --> 00:34:01.023
I think that's true.

00:34:01.023 --> 00:34:04.727
What doesn't kill you
does make you stronger!

00:34:04.727 --> 00:34:07.803
That doesn't mean it
doesn't hurt, it hurts.

00:34:07.803 --> 00:34:10.225
But it makes you stronger.

00:34:10.225 --> 00:34:15.129
And I will tell you, it's
the struggle for the past,

00:34:15.129 --> 00:34:17.428
since 1988, when I got
involved in network marketing,

00:34:17.428 --> 00:34:20.876
it's the struggle that forced me to become

00:34:20.876 --> 00:34:22.659
the person that I am today, and I'm proud

00:34:22.659 --> 00:34:24.986
of the person that I am today.

00:34:24.986 --> 00:34:26.843
Without the struggle, if
it would have been easy

00:34:26.843 --> 00:34:28.535
every single day, I
wouldn't have become much.

00:34:28.535 --> 00:34:31.521
I would have been just an immature idiot

00:34:31.521 --> 00:34:33.597
running around with money,

00:34:33.597 --> 00:34:36.614
versus somebody who's learned and grown,

00:34:36.614 --> 00:34:39.088
and expanded and gotten better.

00:34:39.088 --> 00:34:42.326
Because, even though I had those
days when I wanted to quit,

00:34:42.326 --> 00:34:44.261
I found a reason to stay.

00:34:44.261 --> 00:34:45.944
I found a reason to keep going,

00:34:45.944 --> 00:34:47.861
I found a reason to work through my fears.

00:34:47.861 --> 00:34:51.425
I found a way to conquer the struggle.

00:34:51.425 --> 00:34:53.966
So I don't know where
I find you on this day,

00:34:53.966 --> 00:34:56.205
when this message finds you,

00:34:56.205 --> 00:35:00.301
but if it's landing on you
on a particularly bad day,

00:35:00.301 --> 00:35:01.313
just understand this.

00:35:01.313 --> 00:35:02.160
There's always a reason to quit,

00:35:02.160 --> 00:35:05.577
but there's also always a reason to stay.

00:35:08.159 --> 00:35:09.535
- Thank you guys so much for watching,

00:35:09.535 --> 00:35:12.754
I made this video because
Josue O'Remiggio asked me to,

00:35:12.754 --> 00:35:14.648
so if there's a famous
entrepreneur that you want me

00:35:14.648 --> 00:35:16.769
to profile next, leave
it in the comments below

00:35:16.769 --> 00:35:17.860
and I'll see what I can do.

00:35:17.860 --> 00:35:19.481
I'd also love to know what did Eric say

00:35:19.481 --> 00:35:21.450
that had the biggest
impact on you, what are you

00:35:21.450 --> 00:35:22.869
going to take from this video,

00:35:22.869 --> 00:35:24.780
that you're going to
immediately apply to your life

00:35:24.780 --> 00:35:26.012
or to your business?

00:35:26.012 --> 00:35:28.675
Leave it in the comments, I'm
going to join in the discussion.

00:35:28.675 --> 00:35:30.740
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Total Greatness,

00:35:30.740 --> 00:35:32.931
thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:35:32.931 --> 00:35:36.217
Your One Word, and posting
that fun picture to Instagram,

00:35:36.217 --> 00:35:38.091
I really really really appreciate it.

00:35:38.091 --> 00:35:39.372
So thank you guys again for watching,

00:35:39.372 --> 00:35:42.479
I believe in you, hope you
continue to believe in yourself,

00:35:42.479 --> 00:35:45.489
and whatever your one word is, much love,

00:35:45.489 --> 00:35:46.964
I'll see you soon.

00:35:46.964 --> 00:35:49.964
(loud wind blowing)

00:35:52.836 --> 00:35:56.478
- That Jim Rohn had a
major impact on my life

00:35:56.478 --> 00:36:00.022
by implanting these ideas,
the power of an idea,

00:36:00.022 --> 00:36:02.181
these ideas into my mind.

00:36:02.181 --> 00:36:06.080
Self-education will make you a fortune.

00:36:06.080 --> 00:36:07.653
So a formal education,
everybody goes through,

00:36:07.653 --> 00:36:09.737
you kind of have to go through that.

00:36:09.737 --> 00:36:14.529
But what are you going to do
after formal education is done?

00:36:14.529 --> 00:36:17.466
Self education will make you a fortune.

00:36:17.466 --> 00:36:19.950
And I went, wow, okay.

00:36:19.950 --> 00:36:22.135
He was the one that had me start, cause I,

00:36:22.135 --> 00:36:24.635
back then, if I read any book,

00:36:25.823 --> 00:36:28.339
within about two pages I
was ready to go to sleep.

00:36:28.339 --> 00:36:30.167
I was just exhausted, you know, just like.

00:36:30.167 --> 00:36:31.237
(fake snoring)

00:36:31.237 --> 00:36:35.004
But he said, "Eric, just start
by reading 10 pages a day.

00:36:35.004 --> 00:36:37.284
"Find a book that interests
you, read 10 pages a day.

00:36:37.284 --> 00:36:39.663
"You can get through a 300
page book in a month if you

00:36:39.663 --> 00:36:42.093
"do that, and start to
develop the discipline."

00:36:42.093 --> 00:36:44.345
Because I started just
listening to audio programs.

00:36:44.345 --> 00:36:46.957
I did not have any discipline to read.

00:36:46.957 --> 00:36:49.532
And he made me become a reader, he said,

00:36:49.532 --> 00:36:51.075
"Readers are leaders."

00:36:51.075 --> 00:36:54.168
Self education, what are you
doing to improve your skills

00:36:54.168 --> 00:36:56.805
all the time, are you taking charge?

00:36:56.805 --> 00:36:58.721
And I'm, one of the
things I'm most proud of,

00:36:58.721 --> 00:37:00.671
is how much I've educated myself

00:37:00.671 --> 00:37:03.171
since I left formal education.

00:37:04.771 --> 00:37:07.092
How much I've educated myself,
how many books I've read,

00:37:07.092 --> 00:37:08.827
how many seminars I've gone to,

00:37:08.827 --> 00:37:10.757
how many skills I've
worked on and developed,

00:37:10.757 --> 00:37:13.707
how many coaches I've had and
mentors I've had in my life

00:37:13.707 --> 00:37:15.991
in order to be able to get better.

00:37:15.991 --> 00:37:17.904
Self education will make you a fortune,

00:37:17.904 --> 00:37:19.965
formal education will make you a living,

00:37:19.965 --> 00:37:21.583
you get a paycheck.

00:37:21.583 --> 00:37:24.610
Self education, you get
to be financially free.

00:37:24.610 --> 00:37:28.856
I've read probably two
books a week on average

00:37:28.856 --> 00:37:31.106
for the last 20 plus years.

00:37:33.594 --> 00:37:36.857
So, it's a lot of books, a lot of books.

00:37:36.857 --> 00:37:37.942
Why?

00:37:37.942 --> 00:37:41.812
Because Jim Rohn taught me that
self education will make you

00:37:41.812 --> 00:37:46.460
a fortune, and if you stop
growing, you start dying.

00:37:46.460 --> 00:37:48.655
So I want to continue
in that growth pattern.

